[Event "Knight School"]
[Opening "Queen's Gambit"]
[Variation "Queen's Gambit Declined: Albin Countergambit, Lasker Trap"]
[ECO "D08"]
[Character "tactical"]
[Risk "high"]
[EarlyMate "black"]
[Tricks "trap,pin"]
[Themes "underpromotion,pawn-on-e3"]
[RefutedBy "1. d4 d5 2. c4 e5 3. dxe5 d4 4. e3 Bb4+ 5. Bd2 dxe3 6. Bxb4"]
[For "white"]
[Kind "against-us"]
[Opponent "4...Bb4+"]
[Start "1. d4 d5 2. c4 e5 3. dxe5 d4"]

4. e3 $6 { Looks natural: it attacks the pawn on d4 and opens the bishop. But it walks into a trap, so play 4.Nf3. } 4... Bb4+ 5. Bd2 dxe3 6. Bxb4 $4 { Takes a bishop and looks safe, but it loses at once. } 6... exf2+ 7. Ke2 fxg1=N+ { The pawn becomes a knight rather than a queen, because a knight gives check from g1 and a queen would not. White loses the rook on h1 as well. } *
